          "Klipy (GIF search). Only when GIF search is turned on. When you open the GIF picker or search for a GIF, our own GIF service asks Klipy for you. Klipy receives only the words you search for, your app language, and a random number that is the same for all Zrzur users. Klipy does not receive your IP address, your account or anything else that identifies you. Do not type personal information into GIF search.",
          "GIF pictures in the picker, and GIFs in messages, are loaded through our own servers. Klipy therefore does not see who views them, and we do not tell Klipy which GIF you send. When a GIF is sent, our link service fetches it from Klipy once from our server, not from your device. Your browser may keep GIF pictures from the picker in its own cache for up to 24 hours; we do not keep them on a shared cache.",
          "Our GIF service needs you to be signed in, so it knows that a request comes from your account. It does not store your search words. Technical logs of this service are kept for at most 7 days.",
